 a file opens up black's  rook will not be hanging so you don't  have to really hurry up with the  development of the  uh of the light square bishop but you'll  see what i mean by this we have castles  uh and now knight to a5 chasing back the  bishop the bishop to c2 and now g5 so  expanding on the king side and queen  side both bishop to g3 and now knight to  h5 with the idea of just capturing this  bishop but also uh in some lines maybe  the knight can come to f4 it's going to  be a very powerful piece if black wants  to eliminate it maybe we can open up the  g file to be used for attacking purposes  we have a4 now a4 is even nicer as the  knight on a5 is undefended so captures  would allow us to have a  more than one attack so knight captures  on g3 attacking the rook of course fabio  recaptures with the h pawn and knight  back to c6 and now fabi captures on b5 a  captures a captures and now as the  bishop is on a7 our rook and a8 is not  hanging so there you have it we have  night day 3 fabi continues developing  with tempo the b5 pawn is under attack  and now black has to decide  how to react to this do you  just advance the pawn to b4 because  that's often a very good move  or do you go bishop to a6 and defend the  pawn like mr burke did in this game so  here fabi plays bishop to b3 the bishop  will be incredibly useful on this  diagonal and now knight to e7 black  wants to start  advancing the the pawns the c5 sofa be  beats him to it he plays d4 uh and now e  captures on d4 and now although you want  to capture with the c pawn and improve  your center then you just invite black  to play c5 and then black um pretty much  sold all of his problems he has a very  nice bishop pair here uh that's a weird  arrow he has a very nice bishop pair  here and he's gonna have a very  enjoyable game so fabi captures with the  knight uh and this comes now with the  tempo as the b5 pawn is again hanging so  before now  uh opening up an attack on the knight  but also on the rook on f1 so knight to  c4 the only move and now uh you have to  do something because your bishop on a6  is hanging so bishop captures on c4  bishop captures and only now uh burke  castles and now fabi says all right uh i  could capture here this will uh double  my b pawns but i will be up upon so pawn  captures on b4  and now what do you play here uh well  you could consider something like bishop  to b6 just offering a rook trade you are  down upon but it's a double b pawn and  it's not even a pass pawn so you could  capture on d4  you could do a lot of things but black  decides to play d5  offers another pawn for for some  activity and okay fabi accepts it we  have e captures on d5 uh not bishop  captures because you really don't want  to give up your your light square bishop  so pawn captures on d5 and now queen to  d6 but now  there is a problem in this position and  uh even though it seems like black  activated for for the price of a few  pawns uh the position is winning for  fabi uh so feel free to pause the video  and try to find this move while i give  you a couple of seconds  [Music]  so for those of you who are able to do  it congratulations on going for this  incredible idea and for those of you who  just want to enjoy the show it's knight  to e6  no it's not that's joke it's of course  knight to b5 attacking the queen and the  bishop and our rook and knight are now  attacking the bishop twice so the queen  will capture on b4 now attacking the  bishop here on c4 and black was probably  hoping that we might see a draw here  like rook captures and then queen  captures here we we just trade  everything but here fabi just played b3  and this b3 is the important move you  had to see after you decided to play  knight to b5 because now what does black  play the bishop is hanging and you have  to do something the problem is if you  play something like bishop to b6  we simply trade rook captures rook  captures and play queen to f3 and now we  will have incredible pressure here look  at this bishop and queen once we push  this pawn then even the rook might be  hanging on a8 so after something like  rook to f8 getting rid of both threats  now queen f6 going after the h6 pawn and  there's really no good way to defend if  king h7 we just play d6 and that's it  the entire position just falls apart the  knight is attacked the f7 pawn is  attacked if if bishop captures then we  can simply go queen g6 if the knight  moves uh so there really isn't all that  much uh now the queen is no longer  guarding the knight because the pawn is  here the queen can't capture because the  knight guards the pawn so we might see  something like knight to g6 but then  even d captures on c7 we have a  beautiful pass pawn on c7 that's not the  only winning move most of them are  winning but just to give you an idea so  uh just moving the bishop not all that  great so here  we have queen to c5 adding a defender  here but now again queen to f3 and now  what do you play here uh well king to g7  of course he wants to prevent queen to  f6 going after the h6 pawn but now fabi  has rook to a6 now again we're  threatening to bring the queen over to  f6 uh and again bishop to b6 uh  just fails to the same idea captures  captures and then we play d6 and that's  it the rook is hanging the knight is  hanging the f7 is hanging so everything  is just hanging here so after rook to a6  black plays f6 yes this does prevent the  queen from reaching f6 as the rook now  defends it but this is not one of those  positions where it's okay to play f6 and  now fabi uh goes for the absolute  simplest uh idea and that is rook f2a1  triples up here or rather has now a  triple attack on the a7 bishop uh we  defended knight the c8 and now fabi just  plays the uh i believe the most  beautiful move of the game and that is  king to h2 that's it he was in this  position on move 29 that john burke  resigned the game  as there is nothing more to be done here  and it's a it's a it's a remarkable  position because there is not a single  piece that black can move uh you can't  move the bishop the rook hangs you can't  move the rook we're just going to win  the bishop you can't move the knight  because the knight defends the bishop  you can't move the queen the queen  defends the bishop uh the rook is stuck  here guarding this f6 pawn if the rook  moves we're going to capture it so there  is no move black can make here other  than some sort of a silly pawn push and  even if you try to waste the move with  some like rook to f7 to still keep an  eye on this pawn d6 once again wins the  game now this rook is hanging this rook  is hanging everything is hanging and if  you just repeat rook to f8 we don't even  have to capture here we can even play d7  dislodge the knight we can just you know  play anything and it's still completely  winning  so it's a a position that really went  wrong for black uh he had uh  he had a he had a good position for the  most of the game but then at some point  after he decided to well uh probably to  give up this this pawn here or maybe you  could have done something better you  know even sooner uh it's a it's an  active move but uh playing an active  move against fabi that's not really uh  justified it's just not gonna work  because like i said fabi is currently  almost a 2800 player 27  99.8 so that's really really close and  probably he will reach his uh goal of uh  uh again uh joining the 2800 member club  uh after this tournament but we'll see  it's a strong opposition you know it  just because fabi's the highest rated  player here doesn't mean that he's going  to win and uh if you check out the  previous uh championships uh it's never  that simple uh but yeah uh that's the  game hope you guys enjoyed it and that  you've learned a little bit more about  the rue lopez and how wild it really is  i would like to wish a very happy  birthday to ita i hope you have a great  day and many many more to come and of  course filled with